# Without this, `COPY src/ src/` (or `COPY . .`) pulls in whatever bin/obj happen to exist on the
# host from a local `dotnet build`/`dotnet test`. project.assets.json embeds absolute paths to the
# host's NuGet global-packages folder (e.g. /home/<user>/.nuget/packages/...), which do not exist
# inside the build container — so a container restore succeeds, then publish fails looking for a
# package that "isn't there", even though it restored cleanly seconds earlier. This bites on any
# machine that has ever run `dotnet build` outside a container, Docker or Podman alike.
**/bin/
**/obj/

.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/*.user

README.md
*.slnx

# Local secrets and dev overrides never belong in an image.
.env
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.*.local.json
